              text: 'See the example given below: Taste Sweet Sour Salty Pungent Bitter Astringent Ingredients Jaggery Tamarind Salt Green chilli Neem Raw mango Discuss in small groups and identify the food items having at least three different tastes. _______________________ _______________________ _______________________ A Stall of ‘Super Food’ Surbhi and her friends decided to visit a stall of millet foods. Looking at the menu, Surbhi recalled that her grandmother used to eat jowar and bajra roti in winters and jau roti during summers. Millets are rich sources of nutrients. Children were happy to order jowar upma and eat healthy millet based food items. Do you know? The six tastes such as sweet, sour, salty, pungent, bitter and astringent are known as ‘ shad rasa ’ in Ayurveda. Ayurveda suggests that eating balanced food containing shad rasa is good for health. 30-03-2025 09:47:20 30-03-2025 09:47:20 Food for Health Find out more about a millet-based food prepared at your home. How Does Food Help Us? Children were attracted towards a banner which said — “Colours on Plate, Wellness in Life”. Why do we need to eat different kinds of food items? 30-03-2025 09:47:21 30-03-2025 09:47:21 Our Wondrous World Our body requires a variety of food items to stay healthy, energetic, and strong. Food is required for balanced growth of our body. Since no single food contains all the nutrients our bodies need, it is important to eat a variety of foods. Food Groups Food helps in body building. Food provides energy. Food protects from diseases. 30-03-2025 09:47:22 30-03-2025 09:47:22 Food for Health Foods like rice, potato, wheat, maize, banana, apple, sweet potato, honey, millets, etc., are rich in energy.',
